<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salih ibn Mansur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salih ibn Mansur was an Arab of Himyarite descent who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nekor">Nekor</a> on the Rif coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. Around 710 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> granted him the region, where he preached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> tribes. His descendants, the Salihids, ruled the emirate for about three centuries, and his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-ibn-idris">Said ibn Idris</a> built its capital at Nekor.</p></div>
